<body lang=3D"en-SE" link=3D"blue" vlink=3D"purple" style=3D"word-wrap:brea=
k-word">
<div class=3D"WordSection1">
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-f=
areast-language:EN-US">Hi,<br>
<br>
I made the following two PRs to remove paywalled normative references. Payw=
alled crypto specifications is a cybersecurity risk. People should not have=
 to pay to implement or analyze TLS 1.3.<br>
<br>
Editorial updates to references #1369<br>
</span><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language:EN-US"><a href=
=3D"https://github.com/tlswg/tls13-spec/pull/1369">https://github.com/tlswg=
/tls13-spec/pull/1369</a><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US"><br>
Remove normative references to paywalled crypto #1370<br>
<a href=3D"https://github.com/tlswg/tls13-spec/pull/1370">https://github.co=
m/tlswg/tls13-spec/pull/1370</a><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-f=
areast-language:EN-US">#1369 should be editorial. #1370 changes the referen=
ce for some of the ECDH calculation from to [KEYAGREEMENT]. Some of the ECD=
H calculations already references [KEYAGREEMENT]
 and the changed text in 7.4.2. does not contain any RFC2119 language.<o:p>=
</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-f=
areast-language:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-f=
areast-language:EN-US">Cheers,<br>
John</span><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language:EN-US"><o:p=
></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;mso-fareast-language=
:EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<div id=3D"mail-editor-reference-message-container">
<div>
<div>
<div style=3D"border:none;border-top:solid #B5C4DF 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0cm =
0cm 0cm">
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt"><b><span style=3D"col=
or:black">From:
</span></b><span style=3D"color:black">John Mattsson &lt;john.mattsson=3D40=
ericsson.com@dmarc.ietf.org&gt;<br>
<b>Date: </b>Sunday, 2 February 2025 at 12:45<br>
<b>To: </b>Sean Turner &lt;sean@sn3rd.com&gt;, TLS List &lt;tls@ietf.org&gt=
;<br>
<b>Subject: </b>[TLS] Re: I-D Action: draft-ietf-tls-rfc8446bis-11.txt<o:p>=
</o:p></span></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Hi,<=
br>
<br>
</span><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">I am very happy that </span><span l=
ang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">both FIPS 186-5 and
</span><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">RFC8446bis has removed the normativ=
e reference to ANSI X.62. I strongly think RFC8446bis should replace ALL no=
rmative references to paywalled documents.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span><o:p><=
/o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">I think normative r=
eferences to paywalled
</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">crypto</span><span s=
tyle=3D"font-size:11.0pt"> documents is a substantial cybersecurity risk an=
d goes against everything the IETF stands for [1-3].</span><span lang=3D"EN=
-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt"> I looked
 through all normative references in RFC8446bis.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span><o:p><=
/o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">- [DH76] This docum=
ent is freely available at</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">https://ee.stanford=
.edu/~hellman/publications/24.pdf</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">but I have a hard t=
ime seeing this as a normative referce. I think it should be moved to infor=
mal.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span><o:p><=
/o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">- [IEEE1363] This i=
s paywalled. I don't think RFC8446bis should be published with this as a no=
rmative reference. I think this can and should be replaced with NIST SP 800=
-56A or SECG SEC 1</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">.<=
/span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">https://nvlpubs.nis=
t.gov/nistpubs/SpecialPublications/NIST.SP.800-56Ar3.pdf</span><o:p></o:p><=
/p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">https://www.secg.or=
g/sec1-v2.pdf</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt"><br>
Additional comments on references</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbs=
p;</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">- [RFC8996] &quot;*=
** BROKEN REFERENCE ***&quot;</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Something wrong her=
e.</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span><o:p><=
/o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">- [GCM] Should add =
a</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">n</span><span style=
=3D"font-size:11.0pt"> URL</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">https://doi.org/10.=
6028/NIST.SP.800-38D</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span><o:p><=
/o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">- [X690] Should add=
 a</span><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">n</span><span styl=
e=3D"font-size:11.0pt"> URL</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">https://www.itu.int=
/rec/T-REC-X.690-202102-I/en</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span><o:p><=
/o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">[1]</span><o:p></o:=
p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt"><a href=3D"https://=
emanjon.github.io/NIST-comments/2025%20-%20SP%20800-56%20Subseries.pdf">htt=
ps://emanjon.github.io/NIST-comments/2025%20-%20SP%20800-56%20Subseries.pdf=
</a></span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span><o:p><=
/o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">[2]</span><o:p></o:=
p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt"><a href=3D"https://=
csrc.nist.gov/News/2024/nist-to-revise-special-publication-80038e">https://=
csrc.nist.gov/News/2024/nist-to-revise-special-publication-80038e</a></span=
><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span><o:p><=
/o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">[3]</span><o:p></o:=
p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt"><a href=3D"https://=
csrc.nist.gov/csrc/media/projects/crypto-publication-review-project/documen=
ts/decision-proposal-comments/sp800-38e-decision-proposal-comments-2023.pdf=
">https://csrc.nist.gov/csrc/media/projects/crypto-publication-review-proje=
ct/documents/decision-proposal-comments/sp800-38e-decision-proposal-comment=
s-2023.pdf</a></span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span><o:p><=
/o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt"><span lang=3D"EN-US" =
style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Cheers,<br>
John</span><o:p></o:p></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:12.0pt">On 2024-09-16, 18:08,=
 &quot;Sean Turner&quot; &lt;sean@sn3rd.com&gt; wrote:<o:p></o:p></p>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">This version addresses all known issues. I will bein=
g work on the write-up, but I would expect it to be with our AD by next wee=
k.<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">spt<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt; On Sep 14, 2024, at 16:19, <a href=3D"mailto:in=
ternet-drafts@ietf.org">
internet-drafts@ietf.org</a> wrote:<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt; <o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt; Internet-Draft draft-ietf-tls-rfc8446bis-11.txt=
 is now available. It is a work<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt; item of the Transport Layer Security (TLS) WG o=
f the IETF.<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt; <o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; Title:&nbsp;&nbsp; The Transport La=
yer Security (TLS) Protocol Version 1.3<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; Author:&nbsp;&nbsp;Eric Rescorla<o:=
p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;draft-=
ietf-tls-rfc8446bis-11.txt<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; Pages:&nbsp;&nbsp; 160<o:p></o:p></=
p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; Dates:&nbsp;&nbsp; 2024-09-14<o:p><=
/o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt; <o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt; Abstract:<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt; <o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; This document specifies version 1.3=
 of the Transport Layer Security<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; (TLS) protocol.&nbsp;&nbsp;TLS allo=
ws client/server applications to communicate<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; over the Internet in a way that is =
designed to prevent eavesdropping,<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; tampering, and message forgery.<o:p=
></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt; <o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; This document updates RFCs 5705, 60=
66, 7627, and 8422 and obsoletes<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; RFCs 5077, 5246, 6961, 8422, and 84=
46.&nbsp;&nbsp;This document also specifies<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt;&nbsp;&nbsp; new requirements for TLS 1.2 implem=
entations.<o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&gt; <o:p></o:p></p>
</div>
<div>
